# palette_postfix_bytes_2026-06-11.tsv — issue #69 item 2 A/B (post side)
#
# Question: does the full-image palette transform on the lossless
# multi-group path (dd6b393f) move bytes on natural content?
#
# baseline: benchmarks/lz77_postfix_bytes_2026-06-10.tsv — produced by the
#   b6004d45-equivalent binary; byte-identical to the pre-palette encoder
#   for every cell (the lz77 fix moved nothing on this set; verified
#   129/129 vs its own baseline).
# postfix binary: workspace jxl-encoder--palmg (palette commit dd6b393f
#   lineage; capture binary predates the nc>=2 restriction, which is
#   byte-relevant ONLY for Gray8 inputs where ChannelCompact's density
#   filter declines — zero gray cells moved, so the capture equals the
#   shipped binary's output on every cell).
# host: 7950X WSL2, nice -n19, --threads 8 (bytes thread-invariant)
# grid: 43 images x e{7,8,9} = 129 cells, lossless
#
# VERDICT: 3 moved / 126 byte-identical.
#   7026_plots_line-00081 (aliased-polygons, 14 distinct colours):
#     e7 9,798 -> 6,845 (-30.1%); e8 9,397 -> 6,796 (-27.7%);
#     e9 8,863 -> 6,064 (-31.6%). 3/3 decoders pixel-exact per effort
#     (djxl + jxl_cli/jxl-rs + jxl-oxide).
#   Everything else declines correctly: >1024 colour tuples (photos,
#   ai-art, screenshots at full colour), or single-channel content
#   already covered by ChannelCompact (patents bilevel: full-palette and
#   ChannelCompact are bitstream-identical for nc=1).
# Synthetic floor: 17-colour blocky 512^2 e7 = 3,424 B vs 6,083 B
#   pre-change (-43.7%); locked as hash cell lossless_mg_rgb_512x512_palette_e7.
